00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:26.900
And then, finally,
the location field.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:29.570
Here is the field that contains
two information, the latitude

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:30.320
and the longitude.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:33.230
Those two information
are concatenated

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.100
in the same column.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:38.180
It might be useful for
calculation purposes

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:39.490
to split those two values.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.910
So this is also something
I'm going to do here.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:48.130
I'm going to add a split
step for the location column.

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:57.010
And I'm going to split it using
the semicolon character, which

00:21:57.010 --> 00:22:00.470
is the one that is used to
separate those two values.

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:05.385
So now that's going to create
those two extra columns.

00:22:05.385 --> 00:22:08.010
And to make it easier
to work with that,

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:10.230
I'm going to rename
those columns,

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:25.750
the first one as latitude, and
the second one as longitude.

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:26.250
