00:39:33.240 --> 00:39:35.610
Would the result set in
cache inside of BigQuery

00:39:35.610 --> 00:39:38.130
automatically get invalidated
if the data set changes?

00:39:38.130 --> 00:39:40.005
Somebody has definitely
played with BigQuery,

00:39:40.005 --> 00:39:41.410
and that's absolutely true.

00:39:41.410 --> 00:39:45.152
So cache is invalidated any time
the underlying data changes.

00:39:45.152 --> 00:39:47.610
And the cool thing is, there's
a lot of metadata associated

00:39:47.610 --> 00:39:50.092
with your tables inside
of BigQuery, where

00:39:50.092 --> 00:39:52.050
you can actually look to
see when the table was

00:39:52.050 --> 00:39:53.730
last updated or last modified.

00:39:53.730 --> 00:39:56.716
And you can actually query that
particular metadata, as well.

00:39:56.716 --> 00:39:57.840
I can speak more at length.

