00:40:38.564 --> 00:40:41.460
We have data persisted
in multiple tables.

00:40:41.460 --> 00:40:43.650
Can Dataprep run
on top of BigQuery

00:40:43.650 --> 00:40:46.720
so that we can pull data
from across different tables?

00:40:46.720 --> 00:40:47.520
The answer is yes.

00:40:47.520 --> 00:40:50.220
You can not only pull data
from BigQuery, but also

00:40:50.220 --> 00:40:51.960
from multiple tables.

00:40:51.960 --> 00:40:54.630
You can mix and match
data, coming either

00:40:54.630 --> 00:40:57.130
from cloud storage on BigQuery.

00:40:57.130 --> 00:40:59.710
And you can join those
data sets together.

00:40:59.710 --> 00:41:00.210
So yeah.

00:41:00.210 --> 00:41:02.140
The answer is absolutely yes.

00:41:02.140 --> 00:41:03.295
EVAN JONES: All right.

00:41:03.295 --> 00:41:04.920
When data arrives
periodically, can you

00:41:04.920 --> 00:41:07.740
automate such data
wrangling programmatically

00:41:07.740 --> 00:41:08.745
instead of the UI?

00:41:08.745 --> 00:41:10.620
So you have potentially
a data engineer here.

00:41:10.620 --> 00:41:11.490
JULIEN PHALIP: Yeah.

00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:14.990
So Dataprep is a UI driven tool.

00:41:14.990 --> 00:41:19.280
If the transformations
available in Dataprep

00:41:19.280 --> 00:41:22.570
aren't enough for the
purposes of the work

00:41:22.570 --> 00:41:24.362
you have to do on
your data set, then

00:41:24.362 --> 00:41:26.320
this is where you want
to use DataFlow instead.

00:41:26.320 --> 00:41:30.030
DataFlow is the back
end behind Dataprep,

00:41:30.030 --> 00:41:33.990
which allows you to write down
code that's much lower level,

00:41:33.990 --> 00:41:36.060
but you also have
much more control

00:41:36.060 --> 00:41:38.530
to write very specific
transformations.

00:41:38.530 --> 00:41:39.170
So yeah.

00:41:39.170 --> 00:41:42.140
The answer is that if
those transformations are

00:41:42.140 --> 00:41:45.052
very specific, you would
want to use DataFlow instead.

00:41:45.052 --> 00:41:46.470
EVAN JONES: Great.

00:41:46.470 --> 00:41:48.905
How long does a Dataprep
